{"cuisine/cypriot-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/cypriot-cuisine","n":"Cypriot cuisine","c":"#cf5f87","crumb":[["Europe","cuisines#europe"],["Greek cuisine","cuisine/greek-cuisine"]],"sub":"National cuisine of Cyprus","intro":[["Cypriot cuisine is the cuisine of the island of Cyprus. The cuisine of Cyprus is heavily influenced by neighboring countries like Turkey and Greece. It also has Mediterranean influences because of its position in the Mediterranean Sea, including from countries in the Levant. Halloumi, a staple of the cuisine, traces its name to Arabic."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"cypriot-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cypriot_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Dishes","count":3,"links":[["Fasolada","dish/fasolada"],["Mujaddara","dish/mujaddara"],["Stuffed squash","dish/stuffed-squash"]]},{"h":"Recipe sites","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Kopiaste","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"kopiaste.org","note":"Long-running blog of Greek and Cypriot home recipes.","url":"https://www.kopiaste.org/about/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":2,"rows":[{"name":"My Cypriot Table","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Irene Matys","note":"Greek Cypriot family recipes for sharing and entertaining.","url":"https://penguinrandomhouse.com/books/721737/my-cypriot-table-by-irene-matys","suggested":true,"isbn":"9780525612667"},{"name":"Meliz's Kitchen","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Meliz Berg","note":"Turkish Cypriot comfort food and family recipes.","url":"https://www.penguin.com.au/books/melizs-kitchen-9781473591578","suggested":true,"isbn":"9781473591578"}]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Olive oil","ingredient/olive-oil"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"],["Common bean","ingredient/common-bean"],["Phaseolus vulgaris","ingredient/phaseolus-vulgaris"],["Bulgur","ingredient/bulgur"],["Carum","ingredient/carum"],["Lens","ingredient/lens"],["Lentil","ingredient/lentil"],["Lentils","ingredient/lentils"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Broth","ingredient/broth"],["Ground meat","ingredient/ground-meat"],["Tomato sauce","ingredient/tomato-sauce"],["Zucchini","ingredient/zucchini"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Greek cuisine","cuisine/greek-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"European cuisine","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/5/54/Vin_et_gastronomie_chypriotes.jpg/500px-Vin_et_gastronomie_chypriotes.jpg","w":500,"h":374,"by":"Cyprus Tourism CH","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vin_et_gastronomie_chypriotes.jpg"}},"cuisine/jewish-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/jewish-cuisine","n":"Jewish cuisine","c":"#a99fb5","crumb":[["Cuisine"]],"sub":"Religious cuisine or diet","intro":[["Jewish cuisine refers to the worldwide cooking traditions of the Jewish people. During its evolution over the course of many centuries, it has been shaped by Jewish dietary laws (kashrut), Jewish festivals and holidays, and traditions centred around Shabbat. Jewish cuisine is influenced by the economics, agriculture, and culinary traditions of the many countries in which Jewish communities were displaced and varies widely throughout the entire world."],["The history of Jewish cuisine begins with the cuisine of the ancient Israelites. As the Jewish diaspora grew, different styles of Jewish cooking developed. The distinctive styles in Jewish cuisine vary according to each community across the Ashkenazi, Sephardi, and Mizrahi diaspora groupings."],["Since the establishment of the State of Israel in 1948, and particularly since the late 1970s, a nascent Israeli \"fusion cuisine\" has developed. Israeli cuisine has adapted a multitude of elements, overlapping techniques and ingredients from the many culinary traditions of the Jewish diaspora."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jewish_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Dishes","count":23,"links":[["Appetizing store","dish/appetizing-store"],["Bagel","dish/bagel"],["Brisket (Jewish dish)","dish/brisket-jewish-dish"],["Cebularz","dish/cebularz"],["Challah","dish/challah"],["Forshmak","dish/forshmak"],["Gefilte fish","dish/gefilte-fish"],["Gondi (food)","dish/gondi-food"],["Gribenes","dish/gribenes"],["Hamantash","dish/hamantash"],["Holishkes","dish/holishkes"],["Jewish deli","dish/jewish-deli"],["Lekach","dish/lekach"],["Mafrum","dish/mafrum"],["Matzah brei","dish/matzah-brei"],["Miodownik","dish/miodownik"],["Pizza dolce di Beridde","dish/pizza-dolce-di-beridde"],["Reuben sandwich","dish/reuben-sandwich"],["Shirin polo","dish/shirin-polo"],["Sorrel soup","dish/sorrel-soup"],["Teiglach","dish/teiglach"],["Tsvikli","dish/tsvikli"],["Tzimmes","dish/tzimmes"]]},{"h":"Recipe sites","count":2,"rows":[{"name":"Tori Avey: Jewish Recipes","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"toriavey.com","note":"Tori Avey's Jewish recipe index, often paired with notes on each dish's history.","url":"https://toriavey.com/jewish-recipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"The Nosher (My Jewish Learning)","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"myjewishlearning.com","note":"Recipe section of the nonprofit My Jewish Learning, covering Ashkenazi, Sephardi and Mizrahi home cooking and holiday food.","url":"https://www.myjewishlearning.com/recipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"site"}]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":2,"rows":[{"name":"The Book of Jewish Food: An Odyssey from Samarkand to New York","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Claudia Roden, 1996","note":"Roden's history-rich survey of Ashkenazi and Sephardi cooking across the diaspora.","url":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL22397425M","suggested":true,"isbn":"9780394532585"},{"name":"King Solomon's Table: A Culinary Exploration of Jewish Cooking from Around the World","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Joan Nathan, 2017","note":"Joan Nathan's global tour of Jewish dishes, with recipes gathered from communities on several continents.","url":"https://openlibrary.org/isbn/9780385351140","suggested":true,"isbn":"9780385351140"}]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Yeast","ingredient/yeast"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Carrot","ingredient/carrot"],["Honey","ingredient/honey"],["Papaver","ingredient/papaver"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Ground meat","ingredient/ground-meat"],["Potato","ingredient/potato"],["Raisin","ingredient/raisin"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Wheat","ingredient/wheat"],["Herring","ingredient/herring"],["Matzo meal","ingredient/matzo-meal"],["Whitefish","ingredient/whitefish"],["Besan","ingredient/besan"],["Cardamom","ingredient/cardamom"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Chickpea flour","ingredient/chickpea-flour"],["Dried lime","ingredient/dried-lime"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"],["Ground turkey","ingredient/ground-turkey"],["Lamb","ingredient/lamb"],["Meatball","ingredient/meatball"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."},{"h":"Within Jewish cooking","count":7,"links":[["American Jewish cuisine","cuisine/american-jewish-cuisine"],["Ashkenazi Jewish cuisine","cuisine/ashkenazi-jewish-cuisine"],["Bukharan Jewish cuisine","cuisine/bukharan-jewish-cuisine"],["Ethiopian Jewish cuisine","cuisine/ethiopian-jewish-cuisine"],["Mizrahi Jewish cuisine","cuisine/mizrahi-jewish-cuisine"],["Sephardic Jewish cuisine","cuisine/sephardic-jewish-cuisine"],["Syrian Jewish cuisine","cuisine/syrian-jewish-cuisine"]]}],"cont":null,"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/0/09/Challah_Bread_Six_Braid_1.JPG/500px-Challah_Bread_Six_Braid_1.JPG","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Aviv Hod","lic":"CC BY 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Challah_Bread_Six_Braid_1.JPG"}},"cuisine/mixtec-foodways":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/mixtec-foodways","n":"Mixtec foodways","c":"#94bd5c","crumb":[["The Americas","cuisines#the-americas"],["Native American cuisine","cuisine/native-american-cuisine"]],"sub":"Indigenous foodways, The Mixteca, western Oaxaca and southern Puebla, Mexico","names":"Mixtec","intro":[["The Mixteca has thin soil and few ingredients, so Mixtec cooks get a lot out of ",["corn","ingredient/maize"],", ",["beans","ingredient/beans"]," and ",["chile","ingredient/chili-pepper"],". From Huajuapan de León come chileajo, pork in chile sauce, mole de guajes, made with the pods of the guaje tree, tetelas, large corn tortillas filled with beans, and chilate, a spicy drink of toasted corn, ",["cacao","ingredient/theobroma-cacao"]," and chile. Much of it depends on the chile costeño."],["Goats came with the Spanish, and Mixtec families have raised them for centuries. Each October in the Tehuacán valley of southern Puebla, the matanza turns the year's goats into mole de caderas, a stew of the hindquarters with chile costeño, avocado leaves and guajes. Cooks like Olga Cabrera, from Huajuapan, now take Mixtec dishes to festivals as far away as New York."]],"src":"note","sources":[{"name":"El Universal, Mixtec cuisine delights palates in the US","url":"https://eluniversal.com.mx/english/mixtec-cuisine-delights-palates-us"},{"name":"MexConnect, A yearly culinary ritual, la matanza","url":"https://mexconnect.com/?p=16175"},{"name":"Kiwilimón, What does Mixtec cuisine taste like?","url":"https://us.kiwilimon.com/blog/tips-and-advice/from-kiwilimon-for-you/what-does-mixtec-cuisine-taste-like"}],"actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"mixtec-foodways"}],"sections":[{"h":"Dishes","count":1,"links":[["Mole","dish/mole-sauce"]]},{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[["Native American cuisine","cuisine/native-american-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Key ingredients","links":[["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"]],"note":"Most used across its dishes."},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Native American cuisine","cuisine/native-american-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Cuisine of the Americas","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/3/30/ChickRedMole.JPG/500px-ChickRedMole.JPG","w":500,"h":226,"by":"AlejandroLinaresGarcia","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ChickRedMole.JPG","of":"Mole"}},"dish/amala-food":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/amala-food","n":"Amala (food)","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Yoruba cuisine","dot":"#e46a3f","intro":[["Àmàlà is a staple okele or swallow food originating from and popularized by the Yoruba ethnic group of southwestern Nigeria and other parts of Yorubaland. It is made of yam, cassava flour, or unripe plantain flour. Tubers of yams are peeled, sliced, cleaned, dried and then ground into flour. It is also called èlùbọ́. Yams are white in colour but turn brown when dried which gives àmàlà its colour. It is a popular side dish served with ewédú and gbẹ̀gìrì (black-eyed beans soup), but it is also served with a variety of other ọbè (soups), such as ẹ̀fọ́, ilá, and ogbono."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-amala-food"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amala_(food)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Yoruba cuisine","cuisine/yoruba-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":2,"links":[["Amala","ingredient/amala"],["Yam","ingredient/yam"]]},{"h":"More from Yoruba cuisine","links":[["Draw soup","dish/draw-soup"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/1/10/Amala_and_Abula.jpg/500px-Amala_and_Abula.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Owoeye007","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amala_and_Abula.jpg"}},"dish/american-fried-rice":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/american-fried-rice","n":"American fried rice","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Thai cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["American fried rice is a Thai fried rice dish with \"American\" side ingredients like fried chicken, ham, sausages, raisins, and ketchup. Other ingredients like pineapples and croutons are optional."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-american-fried-rice"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_fried_rice"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Thai cuisine","cuisine/thai-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Ketchup","ingredient/ketchup"],["Processed meat","ingredient/processed-meat"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Hot Thai Kitchen","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"hot-thai-kitchen.com","note":"Pailin Chongchitnant's recipes and videos, with background on technique and ingredients.","url":"https://hot-thai-kitchen.com","suggested":true,"kind":"youtube"},{"name":"SheSimmers","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"shesimmers.com","note":"Bangkok-born writer Leela Punyaratabandhu's blog on Thai home cooking.","url":"https://shesimmers.com/who-is-shesimmers","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Thai cuisine","links":[["Akhuni","dish/akhuni"],["Boat noodles","dish/boat-noodles"],["Drunken noodles","dish/drunken-noodles"],["Evil jungle prince","dish/evil-jungle-prince"],["Fish sauce","dish/fish-sauce"],["Green curry","dish/green-curry"],["Hainanese chicken rice","dish/hainanese-chicken-rice"],["Khanom babin","dish/khanom-babin"],["Khanom chin","dish/khanom-chin"],["Khanom thuai","dish/khanom-thuai"],["Khao soi","dish/khao-soi"],["La tiang","dish/la-tiang"],["Mi krop","dish/mi-krop"],["Miang kham","dish/miang-kham"],["Nam ngiao","dish/nam-ngiao"],["Nam tok (food)","dish/nam-tok-food"],["Pad see ew","dish/pad-see-ew"],["Pad thai","dish/pad-thai"],["Rad naa","dish/rad-naa"],["Rice noodle roll","dish/rice-noodle-roll"],["Sweet chili sauce","dish/sweet-chili-sauce"],["Thai curry","dish/thai-curry"],["Thai fried rice","dish/thai-fried-rice"],["Thali","dish/thali"],["Thua nao","dish/thua-nao"],["Tom kha kai","dish/tom-kha-kai"],["Tom yum","dish/tom-yum"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/c/c3/American_fried_rice.jpg/500px-American_fried_rice.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Biyu Lau","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:American_fried_rice.jpg"}},"dish/butter-cake":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/butter-cake","n":"Butter cake","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from American cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["A butter cake is a cake in which one of the main ingredients is butter. It is baked with basic ingredients: butter, sugar, eggs, flour and leavening agents such as baking powder or baking soda. It is considered one of the quintessential cakes in American baking. Butter cake originated from the English pound cake, which traditionally used equal amounts of butter, flour, sugar, and eggs to bake a heavy, rich cake."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-butter-cake"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Butter_cake"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":4,"links":[["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"]]},{"h":"More from American cuisine","links":[["Angel food cake","dish/angel-food-cake"],["Banana bread","dish/banana-bread"],["Banana pudding","dish/banana-pudding"],["Barbecue sauce","dish/barbecue-sauce"],["Beer cake","dish/beer-cake"],["Better than sex cake","dish/better-than-sex-cake"],["Blini","dish/blini"],["Blooming onion","dish/blooming-onion"],["Brown Betty (dessert)","dish/brown-betty-dessert"],["Brunswick stew","dish/brunswick-stew"],["Buffalo wing","dish/buffalo-wing"],["Caesar salad","dish/caesar-salad"],["Caramel apple","dish/caramel-apple"],["Carbonara","dish/carbonara"],["Cheesesteak","dish/cheesesteak"],["Chicago-style hot dog","dish/chicago-style-hot-dog"],["Chicken nugget","dish/chicken-nugget"],["Chiffon cake","dish/chiffon-cake"],["Chili con carne","dish/chili-con-carne"],["Chimichanga","dish/chimichanga"],["Chow-chow (food)","dish/chow-chow-food"],["Chowder","dish/chowder"],["Cioppino","dish/cioppino"],["Clam chowder","dish/clam-chowder"],["Clam dip","dish/clam-dip"],["Club sandwich","dish/club-sandwich"],["Cobb salad","dish/cobb-salad"],["Cobbler (food)","dish/cobbler-food"],["Cook's Corner","dish/cook-s-corner"],["Crab cake","dish/crab-cake"],["Croffle","dish/croffle"],["Dagwood Bumstead","dish/dagwood-bumstead"],["Dagwood sandwich","dish/dagwood-sandwich"],["Deep-dish pizza","dish/deep-dish-pizza"],["Desperation pie","dish/desperation-pie"],["Dirty rice","dish/dirty-rice"],["Donut hole","dish/donut-hole"],["Egg in the basket","dish/egg-in-the-basket"],["Fish and chips","dish/fish-and-chips"],["Fritter","dish/fritter"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/e/ef/Hazelnut_brown_butter_cake.jpg/500px-Hazelnut_brown_butter_cake.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Justin Grimes","lic":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hazelnut_brown_butter_cake.jpg"}},"dish/canada-bread":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/canada-bread","n":"Cañada bread","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Aragonese cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Pan de cañada (\"drovers' road bread\" in Spanish), or simply cañada, is a variety of torta (flatbread) typical from the center and south of Aragon, in north Spain. It has an elongated and rounded shape, very variable in size, with characteristic grooves in the form of acanaladuras ('channels') or hoyuelos ('dimples') on its surface to cover it with extra virgin olive oil. Its crumb is very moist and spongy, with abundant irregular poring. Its crust is golden, shiny, thin and slightly crunchy. Cañadas can be sweet or savory. Depending on the town, or even the baker, this flatbread can have a rectangular, elliptical or oval shape, with greater or lesser size."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-canada-bread"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ca%C3%B1ada_bread"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Aragonese cuisine","cuisine/aragonese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"More from Aragonese cuisine","links":[["Chistorra","dish/chistorra"],["Regañao","dish/reganao"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/5/54/Sequillo_con_azucar_de_Mora_de_Rubielos_-_Pan_Ca%C3%B1ada_-_2.jpeg/500px-Sequillo_con_azucar_de_Mora_de_Rubielos_-_Pan_Ca%C3%B1ada_-_2.jpeg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Coentor","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sequillo_con_azucar_de_Mora_de_Rubielos_-_Pan_Ca%C3%B1ada_-_2.jpeg"}},"ingredient/iceberg-lettuce":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/iceberg-lettuce","n":"Iceberg lettuce","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 2 dishes across 2 cuisines","intro":[["Iceberg lettuce, also called crisphead lettuce, is a common cultivar of lettuce. Created in 1894 in the United States by Burpee Seeds and Plants, it has since become a staple type of lettuce consumed globally."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-iceberg-lettuce"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Iceberg_lettuce"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine",[["Cobb salad","dish/cobb-salad"]]],["Western American cuisine","cuisine/cuisine-of-the-western-united-states",[["Crab Louie","dish/crab-louie"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Tomato","ingredient/tomato"],["Avocado","ingredient/avocado"],["Bacon","ingredient/bacon"],["Blue cheese","ingredient/blue-cheese"],["Cheese","ingredient/cheese"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Chicken breast","ingredient/chicken-breast"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Lactuca","ingredient/lactuca"],["Romaine lettuce","ingredient/romaine-lettuce"],["Vinaigrette","ingredient/vinaigrette"],["Asparagus","ingredient/asparagus"],["Crab meat","ingredient/crab-meat"],["Hard-boiled egg","ingredient/hard-boiled-egg"],["Louis dressing","ingredient/louis-dressing"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/a/a5/Iceberg_lettuce_%28IJssla_krop%29.jpg/500px-Iceberg_lettuce_%28IJssla_krop%29.jpg","w":500,"h":376,"by":"Rasbak 13:13, 20 May 2007 (UTC)","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Iceberg_lettuce_(IJssla_krop).jpg"}},"ingredient/patty":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/patty","n":"Patty","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["A patty is a flattened, usually round, serving of ground meat or legumes, grains, vegetables, or meat alternatives. Common ground meat used include beef, chicken, and salmon. Patties are found in multiple cuisines throughout the world."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-patty"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patty"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine",[["Hamburger","dish/hamburger"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Cheese","ingredient/cheese"],["Ground meat","ingredient/ground-meat"],["Lettuce","ingredient/lettuce"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/5/52/Hamburger_patty.jpg/500px-Hamburger_patty.jpg","w":500,"h":212,"by":"Lucas, cropped from PDphoto.org","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hamburger_patty.jpg"}},"ingredient/european-perch":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/european-perch","n":"European perch","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["The European perch (Perca fluviatilis), also known as the common perch, redfin perch, big-scaled redfin, English perch, Euro perch, Eurasian perch, Eurasian river perch, Hatch, poor man's rockfish or in Anglophone parts of Europe, simply the perch, is a predatory freshwater fish native to Europe and North Asia. It is the type species of the genus Perca."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-european-perch"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/European_perch"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Finnish cuisine","cuisine/finnish-cuisine",[["Kalakukko","dish/kalakukko"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Coregonus albula","ingredient/coregonus-albula"],["Fish fillet","ingredient/fish-fillet"],["Pork belly","ingredient/pork-belly"],["Rye flour","ingredient/rye-flour"],["Salmon","ingredient/salmon"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/1/1f/Perca_fluviatilis_-_Perche_commune_-_European_perch_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Perca_fluviatilis_-_Perche_commune_-_European_perch_%28cropped%29.jpg","w":500,"h":364,"by":"Gilles San Martin","lic":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Perca_fluviatilis_-_Perche_commune_-_European_perch_(cropped).jpg"}},"dish/kemplang":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/kemplang","n":"Kemplang","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Indonesian cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Kemplang is an Indonesian traditional savory fish cracker (krupuk ikan) snack commonly found in southern parts of Sumatra, Indonesia. Kemplang crackers are commonly made of ikan tenggiri (wahoo) or any type of Spanish mackerel, mixed with tapioca starch and other flavorings, sun-dried and then grilled or fried."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-kemplang"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kemplang"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Spanish mackerel","ingredient/spanish-mackerel"],["Tapioca flour","ingredient/tapioca-flour"],["Wahoo","ingredient/wahoo"]]},{"h":"Cook 